'' A WHOLE ARRAY NO CONSTRUCTOR TAKES -- fbc's 99, "No matching overloaded function", measured on
'' fbc 1.10.1 over lines 15-18 exactly: a string and a long array, as an initialiser and in an
'' assignment, against '( byval as long )' and '( byval as double, byval as long )'. The resolver
'' costs an array as its element, so the string array matched nothing and lowering stopped with
'' TKO0994 ("this N_VAR was not compiled", N_AMBIGUOUS for the assignment), and the long array
'' picked '( byval as long )' and passed it the array. See CtorArrayArgBad_ (checkdecide.tiko).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -fmax-errors 100 --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/ctor-array-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: ctor-array-arg.bas(15,15): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: ctor-array-arg.bas(16,15): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: ctor-array-arg.bas(17,6): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: ctor-array-arg.bas(18,6): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 4
